{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Bhāradvāja","html":"<article id='thag2.29'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 2.29 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 2.29 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dukanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Twos </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Tatiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Three </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Bhāradvājattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Bhāradvāja </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Nadanti evaṁ sappaññā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>This is how the wise roar: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sīhāva girigabbhare; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like lions in mountain caves, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vīrā vijitasaṅgāmā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>heroes, triumphant in battle, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>jetvā māraṁ savāhiniṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>having vanquished Māra with his legions. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Satthā ca pariciṇṇo me, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’ve served the Teacher; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>dhammo saṅgho ca pūjito; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’ve honored the Dhamma and the Saṅgha; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ahañca vitto sumano, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’m happy and joyful, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>puttaṁ disvā anāsavan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>because I’ve seen my son free of defilements. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Bhāradvājo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
